--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,4 +6,6 @@
 
 The function returns a list of at most `limit` products, best first, each with `id`, `name`, `price`, `rating` and `reason` (one line of at most 80 characters, shown under the product). Only products that exist in the catalogue and are in stock are returned, each one once. A blank search, or a catalogue with nothing in stock, gives an empty list.
 
+The reason must not contradict the catalogue. The model is asked not to mention prices, ratings, numbers or rankings on price or rating, and any reason that still does (digits, currency, "under", "top-rated", "best value", "cheapest" and similar) is replaced with an empty string, so the product is shown without a reason rather than with a wrong one. This is a filter on words, so it cannot catch every possible paraphrase.
+
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest` from this directory.
--- a/seam.py
